        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In mammals, L-DOPA can act as a cofactor for the catalyzed reaction; therefore in some resources L-DOPA is shown on both sides of the reaction. GO:0004503 describes the monooxygenation of the monophenol, L-tyrosine. For oxidation of diphenols (including L-DOPA and dopamine), consider instead the term &apos;catechol oxidase activity ; GO:0004097&apos; and its children.</rdfs:comment>
