        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0048869"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The process in which relatively unspecialized cells, e.g. embryonic or regenerative cells, acquire specialized structural and/or functional features that characterize the cells, tissues, or organs of the mature organism or some other relatively stable phase of the organism&apos;s life history. Differentiation includes the processes involved in commitment of a cell to a specific fate and its subsequent development to the mature state.</obo:IAO_0000115>
