        <rdfs:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Transmembrane transport requires transport of a solute across a lipid bilayer. Note that transport through the nuclear pore complex is not transmembrane because the nuclear membrane is a double membrane and is not traversed. For transport through the nuclear pore, consider instead the term &apos;nucleocytoplasmic transport ; GO:0006913&apos; and its children. Note also that this term is not intended for use in annotating lateral movement within membranes.</rdfs:comment>
